-Well.

1787
01:01:56,047 --> 01:01:57,082
-So, uh, scotch?

1788
01:02:01,418 --> 01:02:03,788
-Look, I need help.

1789
01:02:03,822 --> 01:02:04,988
I'm Red Buttons.

1790
01:02:05,022 --> 01:02:08,058
-I just found out that Benson's
hired a killer to get me.

1791
01:02:08,092 --> 01:02:09,793
He's after Joe, too.

1792
01:02:09,827 --> 01:02:11,595
-Well then drink up and get out.

1793
01:02:11,628 --> 01:02:13,530
I don't want no
trouble around place.

1794
01:02:13,563 --> 01:02:14,965
-You're a real pal.

1795
01:02:15,032 --> 01:02:17,033
-Drink up and get out, I said.

1796
01:02:17,067 --> 01:02:19,803
-Packed with minerals,
Booze really satisfies.

1797
01:02:19,837 --> 01:02:21,638
-Ooh, could I lick the glass?

1798
01:02:21,672 --> 01:02:22,407
-Oh, Wendy.

1799
01:02:29,113 --> 01:02:30,982
-A directory for the alley.

1800
01:02:31,015 --> 01:02:32,717
-Well, each bum has
a listing, there.

1801
01:02:32,750 --> 01:02:34,185
-Look at all the neat shops.

1802
01:02:39,690 --> 01:02:41,858
(IMITATING SEDUCTIVE FEMALE
VOICE) Going up, Mr. Chaney?

1803
01:02:41,892 --> 01:02:44,762
-Uh, next up, the food court--
Taco John's, One Potato, Two,

1804
01:02:44,795 --> 01:02:48,098
Great American Hotdog
Experience, Puffy's.

1805
01:02:48,132 --> 01:02:48,698
-Puffy's?

1806
01:02:51,668 --> 01:02:55,038
-Well, I may be indestructible,
but I'm ruled by my tummy.

1807
01:02:55,072 --> 01:02:57,073
[CHUCKLES] It says lunchtime.

1808
01:02:57,107 --> 01:02:59,677
-Hey, could you imagine
a big indestructible snag

1809
01:02:59,710 --> 01:03:00,110
off this thing?

1810
01:03:00,143 --> 01:03:00,645
-Oh, yuck.

1811
01:03:00,678 --> 01:03:01,212
-It'd kill somebody.

1812
01:03:01,245 --> 01:03:02,112
-Snicker-snag Triple.

1813
01:03:06,017 --> 01:03:06,517
-Hey!

1814
01:03:06,550 --> 01:03:08,585
That's ocupado, pal!

1815
01:03:11,755 --> 01:03:15,192
-Hey, look he's in
the cleaver den.

1816
01:03:15,225 --> 01:03:16,060
-Oh.

1817
01:03:16,093 --> 01:03:16,927
-Excuse me.

1818
01:03:16,960 --> 01:03:18,897
Just adding a few
loose ends, here.

1819
01:03:21,798 --> 01:03:24,035
-Look, he's casting
Richard Nixon's shadow.

1820
01:03:24,068 --> 01:03:25,102
-Oh, my goodness.

1821
01:03:27,972 --> 01:03:30,173
-[GUFFAWS] (STUPIDLY) Just
gonna steal a few Post-it notes.

1822
01:03:30,207 --> 01:03:31,742
Yep.

1823
01:03:31,775 --> 01:03:33,810
-(MUFFLED) If you'd
like to make a call--

1824
01:03:33,845 --> 01:03:37,013
-He's really very thorough.

1825
01:03:37,047 --> 01:03:44,155
-Now I'm going to rearrange his
filing system. [LAUGHS EVILLY]

1826
01:03:44,188 --> 01:03:47,023
-Looks like he's wearing a
catcher's mitt around his neck.

1827
01:03:50,327 --> 01:03:53,230
-Say.

1828
01:03:53,263 --> 01:03:55,967
-We'll be back after
these messages.

1829
01:03:56,000 --> 01:03:56,667
-Needs a shave.

1830
01:03:59,237 --> 01:04:01,938
-(NEW JERSEY ACCENT)
Jeez, my appendix burst.

1831
01:04:01,972 --> 01:04:02,740
-It's Tom Landy.

1832
01:04:08,245 --> 01:04:09,780
-Squeamy, is that you?

1833
01:04:13,985 --> 01:04:17,187
-[LAUGHS_STUPIDLY] I have a
sweet tooth-- for revenge.

1834
01:04:20,725 --> 01:04:23,427
-Kind of an enigmatic smile.

1835
01:04:23,460 --> 01:04:24,162
-Hello?

1836
01:04:24,195 --> 01:04:24,962
-Watch me rock.

1837
01:04:32,168 --> 01:04:35,873
-Smooth operator-- huh!

1838
01:04:35,907 --> 01:04:38,842
-I mind very much if you smoke.

1839
01:04:38,875 --> 01:04:40,778
[Gunfire]

1840
01:04:40,812 --> 01:04:43,480
-Missed me, missed me,
now you gotta kiss me.

1841
01:04:43,513 --> 01:04:46,250
-Hey, didn't you see the
first part of this movie?

1842
01:04:51,088 --> 01:04:52,390
-Got him.

1843
01:04:52,423 --> 01:04:53,390
-[Screams]

1844
01:04:53,423 --> 01:04:55,960
-Scream all you want,
but take all you scream.

1845
01:04:55,993 --> 01:04:56,827
-[Continues_screaming]

1846
01:04:56,860 --> 01:04:58,828
-Linda Lavin?

1847
01:04:58,862 --> 01:05:01,832
-[Woman_screams]

1848
01:05:01,865 --> 01:05:03,233
-Plop.

1849
01:05:03,267 --> 01:05:07,538
-Yep, he didn't come
out of his tuck in time.

1850
01:05:07,572 --> 01:05:09,207
-Ah, that's nice.

1851
01:05:09,240 --> 01:05:11,208
I'm tired now, but it's
a good kind of tired.

1852
01:05:11,242 --> 01:05:14,112
Ah.

1853
01:05:14,145 --> 01:05:16,380
-Sara, get me my pilot.

1854
01:05:16,413 --> 01:05:17,113
-Operator?

1855
01:05:17,147 --> 01:05:19,017
Get me the police!

1856
01:05:19,050 --> 01:05:20,550
(FRANTICALLY) Police!

1857
01:05:20,583 --> 01:05:21,252
Yes!

1858
01:05:21,285 --> 01:05:23,853
-Did she say please or police?

1859
01:05:23,887 --> 01:05:26,023
-C'mon, boxcars,
baby needs a new pair

1860
01:05:26,057 --> 01:05:27,123
of indestructible shoes.

1861
01:05:30,260 --> 01:05:33,463
-What are they waiting
for, a putty knife?

1862
01:05:33,497 --> 01:05:34,398
-It kinda looks like rice.

1863
01:05:37,100 --> 01:05:38,402
-What's happened?

1864
01:05:38,435 --> 01:05:41,138
-Guy named Squeamy got
thrown from the fifth floor.

1865
01:05:41,138 --> 01:05:42,340
-Now they call him Squishy.

1866
01:05:42,373 --> 01:05:43,373
-Customer of mine.

1867
01:05:43,407 --> 01:05:43,940
-Tuh!

1868
01:05:43,975 --> 01:05:44,908
-You mean Squeamy Ellis?

1869
01:05:44,942 --> 01:05:45,608
-Yeah, that's him.

1870
01:05:45,643 --> 01:05:46,843
-How many Squeamies do you know?

1871
01:05:46,877 --> 01:05:47,512
-Just Squeamy?

1872
01:05:47,545 --> 01:05:48,612
No-- No one else was killed.

1873
01:05:48,645 --> 01:05:50,613
-Ain't one enough?

1874
01:05:50,648 --> 01:05:53,283
-Wow, everybody's so touchy
at the scene of a death.

1875
01:05:56,587 --> 01:06:00,357
-Hulk, you pull the
car over right now.

1876
01:06:00,390 --> 01:06:02,527
-I tell you, the bullets
never even phased him.

1877
01:06:02,560 --> 01:06:04,162
-Ah, the whole cast is there.

1878
01:06:04,195 --> 01:06:06,097
-Wow.

1879
01:06:06,130 --> 01:06:07,632
-God help us if the
papers get a hold of this.

1880
01:06:07,665 --> 01:06:09,433
-(IRISH ACCENT) All right,
gather around, everybody.

1881
01:06:09,467 --> 01:06:10,233
Lots to see.

1882
01:06:10,267 --> 01:06:11,635
Show's just starting.

1883
01:06:11,668 --> 01:06:13,170
-We're gonna stake out
on Joe Marcellia's.

1884
01:06:13,203 --> 01:06:14,172
-John Huston.

1885
01:06:14,205 --> 01:06:15,072
-No.

1886
01:06:15,105 --> 01:06:17,007
-Lauder, I'm going
to call San Quentin.

1887
01:06:17,040 --> 01:06:18,575
Suppose Benton is alive.

1888
01:06:18,608 --> 01:06:21,145
-Every available man's
been put on the case now.

1889
01:06:21,178 --> 01:06:21,545
Yes, sir.

1890
01:06:21,578 --> 01:06:23,080
All right.

1891
01:06:23,113 --> 01:06:24,448
All right!

1892
01:06:24,482 --> 01:06:25,648
Anything new?

1893
01:06:25,683 --> 01:06:27,050
-Well, remember when I got
ahead of myself a while back?

1894
01:06:27,083 --> 01:06:28,052
Well, we're at that scene now.

1895
01:06:28,085 --> 01:06:30,253
-San Francisco police
located his laboratory

1896
01:06:30,287 --> 01:06:32,423
in the basement of an electrical
power receiving station.

1897
01:06:32,457 --> 01:06:33,657
-Bradshaw, what's he know?

1898
01:06:33,690 --> 01:06:34,492
-He's dead.

1899
01:06:34,525 --> 01:06:36,593
And another man
too, his assistant.

1900
01:06:36,627 --> 01:06:38,128
The lab is a shambles.

1901
01:06:38,162 --> 01:06:39,197
-So's my heart.

1902
01:06:39,230 --> 01:06:41,498
-Now we're getting some
action from San Francisco.

1903
01:06:41,532 --> 01:06:43,933
Benton's body never
arrived at the mortuary

1904
01:06:43,967 --> 01:06:45,302
where it was supposed to go.

1905
01:06:45,335 --> 01:06:47,538
An attendant there
finally broke down--

1906
01:06:47,572 --> 01:06:49,040
-That's not a very good poem.

1907
01:06:49,073 --> 01:06:50,340
Meter's all wrong.

1908
01:06:50,340 --> 01:06:52,610
-By handing the body over to a
man he was unable to identify.

1909
01:06:52,643 --> 01:06:54,745
The man was driving
a station wagon.

1910
01:06:54,778 --> 01:06:57,615
-Oh my god, that's a symbol
of American suburban life!

1911
01:06:57,648 --> 01:06:59,683
-The commissioner's are on his,
and the mayor's are on theirs.

1912
01:06:59,717 --> 01:07:02,720
Now am I supposed to tell them
that our killer is a dead man?

1913
01:07:02,753 --> 01:07:05,522
-They found a notebook
in Bradshaw's lab.

1914
01:07:05,555 --> 01:07:06,757
-It said, [SCREAM].

1915
01:07:06,790 --> 01:07:09,193
-With a professor
Dwiggins at Caltech.

1916
01:07:09,227 --> 01:07:11,128
I hope to hear
from Dwiggins soon.

1917
01:07:11,162 --> 01:07:13,197
-Captain, report
from the Valley,

1918
01:07:13,230 --> 01:07:14,030
on the hysterical woman.

1919
01:07:14,065 --> 01:07:15,298
Reports the presence
of the killer.

1920
01:07:15,332 --> 01:07:16,533
-Oh, that was me.

1921
01:07:16,567 --> 01:07:18,002
Excuse me.

1922
01:07:18,035 --> 01:07:20,037
-Let's go.

1923
01:07:20,070 --> 01:07:21,472
-(SINGING) There's a
monster in the valley,

1924
01:07:21,472 --> 01:07:23,073
and he's prowling in the alley!

1925
01:07:23,107 --> 01:07:24,308
-Hey, check this out, Vern.

1926
01:07:24,342 --> 01:07:26,577
When I let go of the steering
wheel, it pulls to the left.

1927
01:07:26,610 --> 01:07:29,413
Isn't that something?

1928
01:07:29,447 --> 01:07:32,115
-We were just
looking for agates.

1929
01:07:32,148 --> 01:07:35,152
-It's Ma Barker's killer brood.

1930
01:07:35,185 --> 01:07:36,587
-OK, blow hard.

1931
01:07:36,620 --> 01:07:37,655
There you go.

1932
01:07:37,688 --> 01:07:39,557
-Now, you and your boyfriend
had a little fight,

1933
01:07:39,590 --> 01:07:41,558
and he got out of the
car to take a walk.

1934
01:07:41,592 --> 01:07:42,627
-Uh-huh.

1935
01:07:42,660 --> 01:07:43,793
-You noticed that he
walked down towards the sun

1936
01:07:43,827 --> 01:07:46,297
fair in the direction where
you've seen those lights.

1937
01:07:46,330 --> 01:07:46,763
-Uh-huh.

1938
01:07:46,797 --> 01:07:47,330
-Before.

1939
01:07:47,363 --> 01:07:47,965
-Uh-huh.

1940
01:07:47,998 --> 01:07:49,567
-What happened then, Miss?

1941
01:07:49,600 --> 01:07:50,733
Please try to tell us.

1942
01:07:50,768 --> 01:07:52,335
-Go! [MAKES TICKING SOUND]

1943
01:07:52,368 --> 01:07:56,840
-Well, I just sat there,
a few minutes, I guess.

1944
01:07:56,873 --> 01:07:58,042
I was pretty mad.

1945
01:07:58,075 --> 01:07:59,610
-(IMITATING FEMALE VOICE) I
was fluffing in my car, OK?

1946
01:07:59,643 --> 01:08:03,613
-There was a loud
crash, like heavy metal.

1947
01:08:03,647 --> 01:08:04,415
-She's only a bust.

1948
01:08:04,448 --> 01:08:06,250
-From down here.

1949
01:08:06,283 --> 01:08:09,720
I got out of the car
to get a better look.

1950
01:08:09,753 --> 01:08:12,823
I heard Jimmy cry out something.

1951
01:08:12,857 --> 01:08:15,192
-You said Jimmy Smits?

1952
01:08:15,225 --> 01:08:16,493
-Then, down here--

1953
01:08:16,527 --> 01:08:17,495
-I wish you'd blink.

1954
01:08:17,528 --> 01:08:18,762
-A patch of lights.

1955
01:08:18,795 --> 01:08:19,297
-It's like blank.

1956
01:08:19,330 --> 01:08:20,497
-That's incredible.

1957
01:08:20,530 --> 01:08:21,532
-Really spooky.

1958
01:08:21,565 --> 01:08:22,467
-Blink, hello!

1959
01:08:22,500 --> 01:08:23,167
Blink!

1960
01:08:23,200 --> 01:08:23,667
-Blink!

1961
01:08:23,700 --> 01:08:24,702
-Bliiink!

1962
01:08:24,735 --> 01:08:26,537
-Like a zombie, blink!

1963
01:08:26,570 --> 01:08:29,440
-A big man lifted Jimmy up--

1964
01:08:29,473 --> 01:08:30,007
-Please!

1965
01:08:30,040 --> 01:08:30,808
-Over his head like--

1966
01:08:30,842 --> 01:08:32,643
-She's stuck in
Marsha Mason mode!

1967
01:08:32,677 --> 01:08:34,545
-Like he didn't weigh a thing.

1968
01:08:34,578 --> 01:08:36,247
-Jimmy screamed.

1969
01:08:36,280 --> 01:08:37,648
Just once.

1970
01:08:37,682 --> 01:08:38,382
-Go!

1971
01:08:38,415 --> 01:08:39,583
-Blink.

1972
01:08:39,617 --> 01:08:41,218
-Please, blink!

1973
01:08:41,252 --> 01:08:41,952
-What's she looking at?

1974
01:08:41,985 --> 01:08:42,920
-I heard it snap!

1975
01:08:42,953 --> 01:08:45,890
-It sounded like celery!

1976
01:08:45,923 --> 01:08:49,793
-Then I-- I started running
till I found the tide.

1977
01:08:49,827 --> 01:08:52,597
They let me use
the phone. [SOBS]

1978
01:08:52,630 --> 01:08:56,533
-But--I didn't have friends
and family! [MOCK_CRIES]

1979
01:08:56,567 --> 01:08:57,467
-Thank you, Miss.

1980
01:08:57,502 --> 01:08:58,035
-[Continues_sobbing]

1981
01:08:58,068 --> 01:08:58,868
-Can I have my tie back?

1982
01:09:02,840 --> 01:09:05,475
-O'Malley, see that the young
lady gets home all right.

1983
01:09:05,508 --> 01:09:06,743
-Does it have to be her home?

1984
01:09:06,777 --> 01:09:09,012
I'm kidding, of course.

1985
01:09:09,045 --> 01:09:11,782
-Paul Lowe, while
driving to his office,

1986
01:09:11,815 --> 01:09:14,852
heard a radio commentator report
the murder of Joe Marcellia.

1987
01:09:14,885 --> 01:09:15,752
And what shocked him most--

1988
01:09:15,785 --> 01:09:16,753
-(SINGING) I want to
know what love is.

1989
01:09:16,787 --> 01:09:18,722
-Was when the broadcast
identified the killer

1990
01:09:18,755 --> 01:09:21,392
as possibly being the Butcher.

1991
01:09:21,425 --> 01:09:23,527
Lowe headed straight for
Eva Martin at the burlesque.

1992
01:09:23,560 --> 01:09:24,395
-But who doesn't?

1993
01:09:24,428 --> 01:09:25,695
-Oh-ho-ho.

1994
01:09:25,728 --> 01:09:26,397
-Oh!

1995
01:09:26,430 --> 01:09:28,298
You gave me a start, Mr. Lowe.

1996
01:09:28,332 --> 01:09:29,600
-Is this where a corsage goes?

1997
01:09:29,633 --> 01:09:30,533
-Well, I'm taking her place.

1998
01:09:30,567 --> 01:09:32,770
I'm gonna wear her costume.

1999
01:09:32,803 --> 01:09:33,770
What's it to you?

2000
01:09:33,803 --> 01:09:35,472
-I asked you, where's Eva?

2001
01:09:35,505 --> 01:09:36,773
-Hey, don't get physical.

2002
01:09:36,807 --> 01:09:37,675
-Let me hear your body talk.

2003
01:09:37,708 --> 01:09:39,577
-Then watch the tone
of voice, buster.

2004
01:09:39,577 --> 01:09:41,745
I told you, little
Eva isn't here.

2005
01:09:41,778 --> 01:09:42,847
-I can see that for myself.

2006
01:09:42,880 --> 01:09:43,980
Where is she?

2007
01:09:44,013 --> 01:09:45,082
-[Giggles]

2008
01:09:45,115 --> 01:09:46,683
-Hmm, looks like she's
wearing Fruit of the Loins.

2009
01:09:46,717 --> 01:09:47,083
-Oh.

2010
01:09:47,117 --> 01:09:47,652
-Oohh.

2011
01:09:47,685 --> 01:09:49,453
-That's where she is.

2012
01:09:49,487 --> 01:09:51,788
-Yes, sir.

2013
01:09:51,822 --> 01:09:53,690
-No sir, Captain Lauder's
still with the mayor.

2014
01:09:53,723 --> 01:09:54,758
-No, I'll get out of
your officer, sir.

2015
01:09:54,792 --> 01:09:57,695
As soon as poss-- yes,
I'm putting the cigarette

2016
01:09:57,728 --> 01:09:58,928
out now, sir.

2017
01:09:58,962 --> 01:09:59,830
Yeah.

2018
01:09:59,863 --> 01:10:01,965
-Yes sir, we-- we
know he's dangerous.

2019
01:10:01,998 --> 01:10:02,967
Every angle.

2020
01:10:03,000 --> 01:10:05,002
-He's the other end of
a Bob Newhart routine.

2021
01:10:05,035 --> 01:10:07,972
-Yes sir, I-- I'll tell him.

2022
01:10:08,005 --> 01:10:10,975
-We'll have to swing by the
7-Eleven and pick him up.

2023
01:10:14,778 --> 01:10:15,812
-Well, Mr. Wiggins.

2024
01:10:20,952 --> 01:10:21,885
-Huh.

2025
01:10:21,918 --> 01:10:23,087
-What the heel are you doing?

2026
01:10:26,857 --> 01:10:29,460
-Here, ma'am, I'll just
wear my cop shoes home.

2027
01:10:29,493 --> 01:10:30,860
-Thanks.

2028
01:10:30,893 --> 01:10:31,928
-(IMITATES FEMALE
VOICE) How come

2029
01:10:31,962 --> 01:10:32,797
there's powdered sugar in them?

2030
01:10:32,830 --> 01:10:34,832
-Hey, cut with the
doughnut remarks.

2031
01:10:34,865 --> 01:10:36,733
-Ah, jokes.

2032
01:10:36,767 --> 01:10:45,175
[Doors closing]

2033
01:10:45,242 --> 01:10:46,743
-OK, Cambot, bring it in.

2034
01:10:46,743 --> 01:10:48,945
I wanna try that Lon
Cheney eye thing.

2035
01:10:48,978 --> 01:10:50,513
Bring it in closer.

2036
01:10:50,547 --> 01:10:51,082
More.

2037
01:10:51,115 --> 01:10:51,682
More.

2038
01:10:51,715 --> 01:10:52,115
Closer.

2039
01:10:52,148 --> 01:10:52,917
Come on.

2040
01:10:52,950 --> 01:10:53,983
Come on, closer.

2041
01:10:54,017 --> 01:10:54,718
Yeah, that's good.

2042
01:10:54,752 --> 01:10:57,053
Ok.

